WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.835 line:0%
-While you're young,
you don't know anything, really,

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.638 line:0%
whereas it is my responsibility
to only grant the wishes

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.807 line:0%
I am sure are good for Rosas.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.909 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.913 line:0%
-So most of these wishes
will never be granted?

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:17.450 line:0%
-Yet I still protect them
like all the others.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.819 line:0%
-Can't you just
give them back instead?

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.920 line:0%
-Excuse me?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.354 line:0%
-The wishes
you're not going to grant.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:25.424 line:0%
You could just give them back.
Then -- I don't know.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.895
The people can try
to pursue them themselves?

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.130
-We're back with Ariana DeBose,
everybody.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.199
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was a clip from "Wish."

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.167
It's a new Disney movie.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.436
-Yeah, it is.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.004
Celebrating 100 years of Disney.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.306
-100 years. So, this cannot
come soon enough for me.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.707
I mean that sincerely.
-Yeah?

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.609
-Because my boys,
the two older ones,

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:45.611
they're old enough
to go to movies now.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.880
Bringing them to the movies is
my favorite thing in the world.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.283
And not all kids movies
are good.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.684
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:55.188
-Well, I think this one is.
-I believe it is.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:58.457
I mean, again, it is obviously
in the safe hands of Disney.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.560
And so what was your mom's
reaction when you told her

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.128
you were going to be
in a Disney movie?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.897
-Oh, she --
I believe it went like this.

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.766
"You're doing what?

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.335
Wow! That's big!"

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.403
-Oh, wow.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.104
-I was like,
"Yeah, it's cool, Mom."

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.073
She's like, "No, it's cool.
But this is big.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.774
That's like the House of Mouse."

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:17.343
-That's very --

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.013
I like when your parents
outside of show business

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.680
want to let you know
how big something is.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.749
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:26.352
It was a great moment.
We've had many great moments.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.588
-So, tell us a little bit about
your character and the film.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:31.291
Do not spoil anything
because I'm going to see it.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.126
-I promise I will not.
-Okay. Thank you.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.261
-But I do voice
the character of Asha.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.029
-Great.
-And she's so beautiful.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.865
Beautiful brown skin,
braids, and freckles.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.300
Come on, now.
-Alright.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.302
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Um, and...

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:45.871
And she lives in
the magical kingdom of Rosas.

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:48.475
And she is so
community-oriented.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.643
She literally
just loves this space

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:54.780
where she believes
wishes can come true.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.584
And she has this encounter
with King Magnifico

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.687
and discovers that things
are not all that they seem.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.390
And she makes a powerful wish

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.460
and kind of accidentally
calls down the Wishing Star.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.197
And they go on this
really cool journey

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.999
of trying to save their --
the community

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:18.505
and make life and the place
that they live better,

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.707
which I think
is kind of indicative

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.243
of the world we live in today.
-That's very nice.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.010
It's very nice,
but it's a solid message

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.146
for the kids and the adults
who are with the kids.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.615
You got to sing one of the songs
at Disneyland.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.417
-I did. I did.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.986
So "This Wish" is what I think

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:37.891
is kind of, like, the mother
of all "I want" songs.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.792
Like, the Disney "I want" songs.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.861
You know, like "Go the Distance"
from "Hercules,"

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.030
that sort of thing.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.432
-And I sang it recently

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:49.535
at Aurora's Castle
at Disneyland.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:50.636
I'd never been.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:52.538
So, cool, cool.
Everything's fine.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:56.843
And it was -- it was so special
for many reasons,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.711
but mostly because I looked out,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.849
and the kids in the audience
were already singing the song.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.883
-That's a trip.
-You know?

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.351
Like, that was --

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.253
It was one of those pinch-me
moments when you realize,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.755
"Oh, this thing
that I said yes to

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.991
that I, you know,
had so much fun making..."

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:15.694
I put a lot of heart into it.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:20.266
And to see that it's being
received from kids already

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.336
and that they're going to
sing this beautiful music

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.972
and learn from it
is kind of everything.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.940
-That's so lovely.
And it just makes me...

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.842
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.479
-It also -- It also
just makes me dread

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.081
my kids butchering it
in the back seat of the car.

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:38.985
-That's -- See, but I like that.
-You like the butchering?

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.786
-I'm okay -- Well, come on.
How many songs --

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.954
I mean, "Let It Go."

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.223
♪ Let it go, let it go ♪

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.092
Like, it happens, but...
-Yeah.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.028
-But it makes you
feel good inside.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.696
Like, singing in the shower.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:53.165
♪ So I'll make this wish ♪

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:57.369
Like, it's fine. Like,
sing to your heart's desire.

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:59.505
-That is still so much better
than them.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.574
[ Laughter ]
Like, that's very cruel

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.576
that you're like,
"Bad like this."

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.977
I'm like, "Is that bad, though?"

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.446
'Cause I -- I feel like
I would listen to that.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.847
-Oh, no.
-What were your favorites?

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:11.016
What was your favorites
growing up, your Disney movies?

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:13.786
-Oh, I had so many. I --
"Beauty and the Beast."

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.188
I was Belle for Halloween.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.423
I was Snow White
for Halloween.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.325
Granted, I'm giving
Evil Queen vibes today.

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:21.527
Anyone?
-Yeah, it's very good.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.029
-And honestly,
she was very scary.

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:25.898
"Mulan."
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.599
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:30.736
Like, come on. So graceful.
Everything.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.840
"Hercules." The Muses.
Like, what?!

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.008
There are so many.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.076
But wait. You were a Disney kid.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.644
-I grew up with Disney. Yeah.
-So what are your favorites?

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:42.147
-From, like, a different era.
-That's okay.

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:44.016
-"Fantasia." No. Um...

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.185
[ Laughter ]
-Let's take it all the way back.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.387
-These are the ones
that are, like, when I was --

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.957
This dates me, but it's always
the ones I saw in the theater.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.492
So "Jungle Book."
"Sword in the Stone."

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:55.228
"Robin Hood" is one
I really like.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.862
"The Rescuers"
was a big one for me.

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:59.098
-Oh, I love "The Rescuers"!
Medusa?!

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.266
-Yeah. Really good.
Really good villain.

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:03.669
-Really great villain.
Were you into "Tarzan"?

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.204
Because I was into "Tarzan."
-I did enjoy --

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.572
-I feel like I maybe --
You know what?

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.207
I'm gonna be honest.
I think I missed "Tarzan."

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.542
-What? Phil Collins?
"Trashin' the Camp"?

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:11.811
-Yeah.
-What?!

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.846
-I think, though,
there's this time in your life

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.548
between when you're a kid
and when you have them

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:17.884
that you're not like,

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.452
"I got to see
the new Disney movie."

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.786
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.255
-You know,
I don't have children,

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.490
so I'm gonna say
that that's really fair.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.925
-Yeah. But I will say --
You know what?

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:30.229
The one that I missed and then
my kids found is "Moana."

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.899
-So good.
-"Moana" now -- I can't --

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.801
And I've seen it a bunch
because it's their favorite.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.002
You know what's interesting?

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:39.138
My oldest says this about
"Moana," and he's a boy.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.772
He's like,
"'Moana' is my favorite

00:05:40.772 --> 00:05:43.809
because the girl never
talks about true love."

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:44.977
And I'm like, "Look at them."

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.378
And I'm like --
That's really good that

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:48.414
it's, like, not -- like,
there's a female character

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.982
who's just, like, a hero

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.051
and it's not about her
trying to, like, find a dude.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:55.187
-Find love.
And, you know, Asha and "Wish"

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:56.922
is inherently very much
like that, as well.

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:59.792
So, hopefully, your oldest
is going to enjoy it, too.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.927
-Yeah.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:05.564
-No, it's exciting when --
There are other stories to tell,

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:06.932
which I think is a good thing.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:10.436
Like, I think what drew me
to "Wish" was the fact that,

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:13.940
like, you're watching
an unsuspecting girl

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.408
step into a leadership role.

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.409
It's not like
she was looking for it.

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.478
She just became it.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.748
And she tries, she fails,
she tries again.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.317
Like, those are beautiful things

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:25.885
that I think children
should learn.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.753
-And, now, is it true
that your karaoke song

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.922
is a Disney song?
-Yes.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.490
-What is it?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.492
-"Colors of the Wind"
from "Pocahontas."

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:35.862
-Oh, wow.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.229
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, come on!

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:40.065
The Vanessa Williams
credit version is everything.

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:41.767
-Wow.
-She said...

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:46.372
♪ Can you paint with all
the colors of the wind? ♪

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.740
So good. Like...

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.875
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.778
-I will be doing that
in the shower tomorrow!

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:54.680
-Yes!
-I cannot wait.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.949
What a delight to have you here.
Thank you so much.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.518
You guys, that's Ariana DeBose.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:01.753
"Wish" is in theaters nationwide
on November 22nd.

00:07:01.753 --> 00:07:04.690
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Iman Vellani.

